WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.500
The SaveBench prototype. Its contestants, designs, events and results are all made up.
The challenge and its shared criteria come first.

00:04.500 --> 00:08.500
Run starts the built-in preview, which plays scripted sample events.
No model, game or server is running.

00:08.500 --> 00:12.800
A1's factory diagram appears with its public plan and event feed.
Its sample iron rod rate is 8 against a target of 10 items per game minute.

00:12.800 --> 00:17.400
The remaining sample events bring in results for A2 and B1.
They show the interface, not measured model results.

00:17.400 --> 00:20.000
A2's result shows its later sample measurements,
which meet both rate targets.

00:20.000 --> 00:23.300
Selecting the older A1 brings back that revision's diagram and result.
Its shortfall stays visible after A2's success.

00:23.300 --> 00:27.000
Compare uses the latest tested revisions, A2 and B1.
Finding B1 on the map shows its different eight-building layout.

00:27.000 --> 00:31.300
The comparison keeps observed differences apart from each contestant's own account.
The sample challenge sets targets, not one overall winning score.

00:31.300 --> 00:33.080
Game artwork was removed from the capture.
The rectangles and routes are the prototype's simple sketches.
